  "label": "Aesthetic Mockery",
  "description": "The meme employs aesthetic mockery — the act of ridiculing someone’s appearance or style — by comparing the person to a Picasso painting. This requires understanding that appearance can be judged or mocked in a humorous context, which is a common social trope, though potentially harmful as it can reduce a person’s worth to their looks.",
